      <!-- Historical Evolution Timeline -->
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        
        <!-- Pre-Colonial -->
        <div class="glass-panel p-5 rounded-xl border-l-4 border-l-amber-500 space-y-3">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase text-amber-400 bg-amber-950/60 px-2 py-0.5 rounded border border-amber-800">1. Pre-Colonial Era</span>
            <i data-lucide="flame" class="w-4 h-4 text-amber-400"></i>
          </div>
          <h4 class="font-semibold text-base text-white">Traditional Thermal & Biological Methods</h4>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            Preservation relied heavily on salting (<em>daing/tuyo</em>), drying, smoking (<em>tinapa</em>), and fermentation (<em>bagoong</em>). While effective for extended shelf life, these methods fundamentally alter the raw state, market value, and freshness of fruits and vegetables.
          </p>
          <div class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 bg-slate-900/60 p-2 rounded border border-slate-800">
            <strong>STS Insight:</strong> Indigenous knowledge adapted to local tropical humidity, but could not preserve live botanical tissue without chemical transformation.
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Industrial Revolution -->
        <div class="glass-panel p-5 rounded-xl border-l-4 border-l-blue-500 space-y-3">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase text-blue-400 bg-blue-950/60 px-2 py-0.5 rounded border border-blue-800">2. Industrial Era</span>
            <i data-lucide="snowflake" class="w-4 h-4 text-blue-400"></i>
          </div>
          <h4 class="font-semibold text-base text-white">Mechanical Vapor-Compression</h4>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            The invention of compressor-based refrigeration enabled active temperature reduction ($2^\circ\text{C}-8^\circ\text{C}$). However, this technology was engineered around centralized urban industrial grids with heavy copper loops, power-hungry AC compressors, and chemical refrigerants.
          </p>
          <div class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 bg-slate-900/60 p-2 rounded border border-slate-800">
            <strong>STS Insight:</strong> Technology created structural urban-rural inequality; cold chains served centralized ports rather than dispersed agricultural highlands.
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Modern PH Crisis -->
        <div class="glass-panel p-5 rounded-xl border-l-4 border-l-rose-500 space-y-3">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase text-rose-400 bg-rose-950/60 px-2 py-0.5 rounded border border-rose-800">3. Modern Philippine Context</span>
            <i data-lucide="alert-triangle" class="w-4 h-4 text-rose-400"></i>
          </div>
          <h4 class="font-semibold text-base text-white">High Electricity Costs & Middlemen Exploitation</h4>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            The Philippines suffers from high electricity rates and frequent provincial blackouts. Smallholder farmers, lacking individual cold storage, are forced to panic-sell produce at cut-rate prices to traders (<em>tradores</em>), causing up to 40% post-harvest spoilage.
          </p>
          <div class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 bg-slate-900/60 p-2 rounded border border-slate-800">
            <strong>STS Insight:</strong> Infrastructure gaps directly trigger agrarian poverty, urban food inflation, and national food insecurity.
          </div>
        </div>

